Caelza: the simplified setup (vision M4 phase 4a), Cael's screens at /setup.

The dashboard's quickstart is upstream's five-section wizard with our two
doors inserted; a new owner still meets a provider dropdown, an alias, a
free-text model box and three profile pickers. /setup is the "dumbed down"
path: Cael leads, one decision a screen, in the brand's own colours. Behind
"bring your own key" a scroll wheel of the providers most people bring
(bundle/models.json, copied beside the page by runtime/build.sh; "more"
adds every other key provider the Runtime lists), a wheel of that
provider's models with Cael's picks pinned on top (best, fast and cheap,
strongest, free) above the Runtime's live catalog, one box for the key,
then "Try it". Behind "free and local" the ladder's pick for this device.
Everything the owner is not asked takes a default and the whole thing goes
through upstream's /api/quickstart/apply, so the result is what the full
wizard would have written; the wizard stays at /quickstart as "Advanced
setup". The page, the wheel and the logic live in the overlay
(web/src/pages/setup/); these hunks route /setup outside the dashboard
chrome, land a fresh install on it instead of /quickstart, put "Set up" at
the top of the sidebar's Configure group, add the strings (English; the
other locales fall back), let tsc import the catalog as JSON and list the
logic test beside the doors'. Applied after 0008 and the overlay copy.

